# Scope-downs pass (apps/api/Dockerfile's first-ever build) — without this, `COPY . .` sends the
# entire repo root as build context, including `target/` (a real, measured 37GB of host Rust
# build artifacts) and `node_modules/` (637MB) — the actual cause of a build that spent 32+
# minutes just transferring context before failing outright. Real, not theoretical.
target/
node_modules/
.git/
.next/
**/node_modules/
**/target/
# A real, second bug found via a live build (not theoretical): apps/api/build.rs looks for a
# local `protoc.exe`/`protoc` in this exact directory before falling back to a system `protoc`,
# preferring it if present. That directory holds a WINDOWS-only `protoc.exe` fetched for local
# host dev (gitignored, never meant to leave this machine) — copying it into a Linux build
# context makes build.rs try to exec a Windows PE binary inside Linux, which fails with a bizarre
# WSL interop error, not a clean "not found". Excluded so build.rs's own fallback (a real
# `protobuf-compiler` apt package installed in the Docker build stage) is what actually runs.
packages/fuml-runtime/tools/
